  "tagline": "Small, fast SPARQL database in Rust that embeds in Rust, Python and JavaScript or runs as a server.",
  "description": "Oxigraph is an open-source RDF graph database and SPARQL engine written in Rust. It stores quads in RocksDB (or in memory), implements SPARQL 1.1 Query, Update and Federated Query with early SPARQL 1.2/RDF 1.2 support, and ships as a Rust crate, a Python package (pyoxigraph), a JavaScript/WebAssembly package and a standalone HTTP server. It is a good default for embedding RDF in applications, notebooks and browsers, or for small-to-medium SPARQL endpoints. It is not a distributed or reasoning-heavy store, and its query optimizer is simpler than those in commercial triplestores.",
